# Possible SQL Injection Attempt - OR Pattern (sid 1391223)
#
# What:    Fires on an HTTP request whose URI contains '+OR+ (case-insensitive),
#          the classic ' OR 1=1 tautology with spaces encoded as "+".
# ATT&CK:  T1190 Exploit Public-Facing Application
# Target:  Lab web app (DVWA) in the AttackLab VLAN.
# Limits:  Narrow, signature-style match. Misses %20 or %27 encoding, comments
#          (/**/), POST bodies, and other SQLi forms (UNION, stacked queries).
#          Unencrypted HTTP only; Suricata cannot see inside HTTPS here.
# Deploy:  Security Onion -> Detections -> add as a Suricata (NIDS) rule, or
#          append to local.rules on any Suricata sensor. Requires $HOME_NET.

alert http any any -> $HOME_NET any (msg:"Possible SQL Injection Attempt - OR Pattern"; flow:to_server,established; http.uri; content:"'+OR+"; nocase; classtype:web-application-attack; sid:1391223; rev:1;)
